Package: cybroid-edition-developer
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: CybroidOS maintainers <citos@cybroid.com>
Homepage: https://cybroid.com/cybroidos
Section: metapackages
Priority: optional
Depends: cybroid-plasma (>= @VERSION@), git, git-lfs, gh, build-essential, gdb, clang, cmake, make, ninja-build, meson, pkg-config, valgrind, strace, shellcheck, python3-venv, python3-pip, python3-dev, pipx, golang, rustc, cargo, nodejs, npm, default-jdk, maven, php-cli, composer, sqlite3, sqlitebrowser, postgresql-client, mariadb-client, redis-tools, httpie, jq, neovim, tmux, ripgrep, fd-find, meld, podman, podman-compose, podman-docker, distrobox
Description: CybroidOS Developer: for engineers who build software
 Toolchains, databases and containers ready on first boot: Git with Git LFS
 and the GitHub CLI; GCC and Clang with CMake, Meson, Ninja, GDB, Valgrind
 and strace; Python, Go, Rust, Node.js, Java (OpenJDK and Maven) and PHP
 (with Composer); SQLite with DB Browser, and PostgreSQL, MariaDB and Redis
 clients; containers with Podman (the docker and docker compose commands
 work too, without a background service or root) and Distrobox; Neovim,
 tmux, ripgrep, fd, Meld, HTTPie and jq. A code editor (VSCodium) installs
 from the App Centre.
 .
 The same CybroidOS as every edition (look, updates, Hangar), with these
 tools added. An installed CybroidOS becomes this edition by installing this
 package; several editions can be installed together.
